language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ appointment_scheduling: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Schedule 4 people into 4 interview slots based on their free-busy schedules, where m[i][j] is 1 if person i is free in slot j. Each person gets exactly one slot in which they are free, and each slot goes to exactly one person.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `appointment_scheduling.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/appointment_scheduling.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `appointment_scheduling_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py appointment_scheduling.json
$   savilerow model.eprime appointment_scheduling_1.param -run-solver

$ the number of people, and the number of interview slots (both 4)
letting people = 4
letting slots = 4
$ m[i,j]: 1 if person i is free in slot j, 0 if busy, indices 1-based
given m : matrix indexed by [int(1..people), int(1..slots)] of int(0..1)

$ x[i,j]: person i is assigned to slot j
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..people), int(1..slots)] of bool

branching on [x]

such that
$ each person is assigned exactly one interview slot
forAll i : int(1..people) . (sum j : int(1..slots) . toInt(x[i,j])) = 1,
$ each interview slot is assigned to exactly one person
forAll j : int(1..slots) . (sum i : int(1..people) . toInt(x[i,j])) = 1,
$ a person is assigned only to a slot in which they are free
forAll i : int(1..people) . forAll j : int(1..slots) . (x[i,j] -> m[i,j] = 1)
